course: dictionary
lesson: 13673
title: Ingress: the way in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ingress is a formal word for going in, or a way in. It can also mean the right to go in. Its opposite is egress, which means going out.
explain: In technical writing, ingress means water, dust or air getting in where it should not. «The phone case has a seal to stop water ingress.» The seal keeps the water out, so it cannot get in.
explain: Look at the words around it. A gate, a door or a tunnel next to ingress means a way in. A seal, a case or a rating next to it usually means something getting in where it should not. Ask yourself: is something going in, or being kept out?
fact: Ingress means the act of going in, or a way in.
fact: Water ingress means water getting in where it should not.
fact: Ingress and egress go together: ingress is going in, and egress is going out.
fact: «The guard blocked the ingress to the tunnel.» Here ingress means the way in.
fact: Ingress is usually used in formal, legal or technical writing, not in everyday chat.
exercise: «The old gate was the only ingress to the garden.» What does ingress mean here? | A loud noise | A way out | *A way in | A tall fence
exercise: «The phone case stops water ingress, so it survives the rain.» What is water ingress? | Water being drunk by the phone | *Water getting in where it should not | A water slide at the park | Water being poured out of a bottle
exercise: Which word means going out, the opposite of ingress? | *Egress | Ingot | Ingress | Engine
test: «Dust ingress can damage a computer inside its case.» What does dust ingress mean? | A dust storm far away | *Dust getting in where it should not | Dust being swept off the table | Dust settling on a shelf
test: «The fire exit gave a means of ingress and egress.» Which word means going out? | Engine | Ingredient | Ingress | *Egress
exam: «The sealed box was built to stop all ingress of water and dust.» What does ingress mean here? | Getting out quickly | Being painted a bright colour | *Getting in where it should not | Being shaken very hard
